-- Known (2026-11-21, from the sessions of 2026-11-20 and 2026-11-21 with Avik): the direction, what
-- was compared, and what serves what.
-- The direction (How to work, its first two items): the machine is written in hyperactive, every
-- part proven; references are by content, never by name; hyperactive compiles out to C, with the C
-- compiler a named assumption until one is proven; there is no OCaml machine, no port of the core C,
-- no Rust, and direct x86 is not on the path. The core C is not refactored: it runs the checker until
-- hyperactive emits its own machine as C, then it is deleted whole; it changes only on Avik's word or
-- to fix what blocks the work.
-- Compared (the comparison the note of 2026-11-13 says nobody had made, for the calculus's rule
-- cases): core.h whole and net.c 380–480, 751–776, 1138–1498, 1862–2609 at 3aed33d6, each rule read
-- against the paper's §3.4 and §4 and CCHM as the paper cites it: application, force, projections,
-- path application, dimension substitution, systems, composition's dispatch on the head of the type
-- family, Glue, constructors with dimensions, composition and transport in data types, case. No rule
-- read disagrees. Not read: what the dispatch calls (the prelude's clauses beyond %comp-pi and
-- %comp-u, the clauses generated per data type), the checker's clauses, words, primitive values, the
-- checker's views. The rules are stated as interactions in Part I §4.5, "The rules as interactions"
-- (blocks s4-5-p1 to s4-5-p10), and in the repository's README.
-- Confirmed defects: with lib/prim.cub loaded a closed proof of Empty is accepted, because byte
-- strings are equal by content (net.c O_BEQ), a store returns a copy (O_STOREC) and ptr-of, typed as
-- a function, returns the copy's address (O_PTROF): the seven definitions are in the handoff
-- document's closing section; read, not re-run. Universe composition is Cubical Agda's (already
-- noted below, 2026-11-12). Reported and not verified here: conversion does not compare the faces of
-- two formal compositions; a composition with an empty tube in a data type reduces to its base
-- (consistent with net.c 2264–2265 and 2364–2369).
-- What is to be done, and what each part needs first. E, a sound checker (the ptr-of hole closed,
-- universe composition and the paper agreeing, the two reports settled, no stored verdict accepted
-- without checking): needs nothing, and every later proof rests on it. S, the store by content
-- (Avik's handoff of 2026-11-20): the store's view as a definition of the language (objects,
-- references by content, names an overlay, dead statements); stored objects referring by content
-- only; no path binding and no merging by name; the regeneration of users when a dependency is
-- replaced (f to f′ gives G to G′, a proof at f carried to G); what a site shows being the content
-- its defining object refers to; the existing source carried over without loss. K, the machine in
-- hyperactive: what a net means as a term, each rule of §4.5 with its proof, then words, primitive
-- values, the checker's views, the world, workers. C, the emitter to C: see hyperactive-emits-c. F,
-- the front end in the language, by the path core-forced-by-paper records as Avik's (each notation a
-- `syntax N` giving meanings, then its C goes): needs S, because it writes what the store holds. X,
-- hyperactive builds itself and the core C is deleted: needs K, C, F and S. E first; then S, K and C
-- beside one another; then F; then X. The factoring of the code that exists (the same thing written
-- twice merged by one proof; declarations with no reason) blocks none of these, and name clashes,
-- texts held under several paths and load-order dependencies stop existing once S holds.
-- Tools written 2026-11-21 over what unexplained reads, all only reading: `hyperactive same-type`,
-- `same-text` (196 pieces of text are held in more than one module, in 2,256 places, 2,010 of them
-- lib/suffix-index.cub with its numbered copies and lib/suffix-query.cub with lib/sq2.cub),
-- `held-whole`, `unimported`, `foldable`, `fold-safe`. A fold that removed the thirteen fold-safe
-- modules made the names they declared stop resolving though other modules declare them, and was
-- undone uncommitted; hy-fold-modules is out of the dispatcher. No command that changes the source
-- is written until the store's view is a definition such a command is proven against.
